# Project conventions

## Tests are paused

Do **not** write, extend or update any tests until the user explicitly asks for them again.
This applies to unit, bloc and widget tests alike, even when `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`
lists tests as part of a phase — skip that part of the phase and say so in the summary.

Existing tests under `test/` stay as they are. If a change makes one fail to compile,
report it instead of rewriting the test.

## Comments

Code explains itself through naming and structure. The only comments allowed:

- short `TODO`s for genuinely deferred work — `// TODO: wire up a crash reporter.`
- a rare one-liner stating a constraint the code cannot show.

No doc comments, no narration of what a class or method does.

## README

Never edit `README.md`. The user writes it at the end.
